{
  "name": "General Info",
  "icon": "nuclearcraft:fusion_core",
  "category": "nuclearcraft:fusion",
  "sortnum": 0,
  "pages": [
    {
      "anchor": "intro",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "$(thing)Fusion reactors$() generate decent amounts of energy by fusing particles together. They can also boil coolants, which must be supplied in order to cool down the reactor's function blocks."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "reactor_design",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Plasma in bigger reactors can reach higher temperatures. A larger reaction chamber can also hold more fuel and produce more energy."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "casing",
      "type": "blocks/2",
      "header": "Reactor Casing",
      "block1": "nuclearcraft:fusion_reactor_casing",
      "block2": "nuclearcraft:fusion_reactor_casing_glass",
      "text": "Reactor casing blocks are used to build the toroidal structure (Reaction Chamber) around the $(item)Fusion Core$()."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "toroidal_section",
      "header": "Toroidal Section",
      "type": "patchouli:multiblock",
      "multiblock": {
        "mapping": {
          "C": "nuclearcraft:fusion_reactor_casing",
          "G": "nuclearcraft:fusion_reactor_casing_glass"
        },
        "pattern": [
          [
            "   ",
            "C G",
            "   "
          ],
          [
            "C G",
            " 0 ",
            "C G"
          ],
          [
            "   ",
            "C G",
            "   "
          ]
        ],
        "symmetrical": true,
        "visualize": false
      },
      "text": "You can use any casing block, or combine them, to build the toroidal section. The center of the section must be empty."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "controller",
      "type": "blocks/1",
      "header": "Reactor Core",
      "block": "nuclearcraft:fusion_core",
      "text": "Without a controller, the reactor multiblock will not form. Its GUI shows information about the reactor, such as the averages of relevant components' stats."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "connector",
      "type": "blocks/1",
      "header": "Fusion Connectors",
      "block": "nuclearcraft:fusion_reactor_connector",
      "text": "$(item)Fusion Connectors$() are used to connect the fusion core to the toroidal reaction chamber. They transfer fuel, coolant, and energy."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "function_blocks",
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "header": "Functional Blocks",
      "text": "The $(thing)Fusion Reactor Chamber$() needs 2 kinds of functional blocks: Electromagnets and RF Amplifiers. These blocks require energy to operate and coolant to keep cool. They must be placed at the corners of the toroidal reaction chamber section."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "electormagnets",
      "type": "blocks/2",
      "header": "Electromagnets",
      "block1": "nuclearcraft:basic_electromagnet,nuclearcraft:bscco_electromagnet,nuclearcraft:magnesium_diboride_electromagnet,nuclearcraft:niobium_tin_electromagnet,nuclearcraft:niobium_titanium_electromagnet",
      "block2": "nuclearcraft:basic_electromagnet_slope,nuclearcraft:bscco_electromagnet_slope,nuclearcraft:magnesium_diboride_electromagnet_slope,nuclearcraft:niobium_tin_electromagnet_slope,nuclearcraft:niobium_titanium_electromagnet_slope",
      "text": "$(item)Electromagnets$() are used to sustain plasma in the reaction chamber. A bigger electromagnetic field means better plasma stability and cross-section. It also means less plasma heat loss."
    },
    {
      "anchor": "rf_amplifiers",
      "type": "blocks/1",
      "header": "RF Amplifiers",
      "block": "nuclearcraft:basic_rf_amplifier,nuclearcraft:bscco_rf_amplifier,nuclearcraft:magnesium_diboride_rf_amplifier,nuclearcraft:niobium_tin_rf_amplifier,nuclearcraft:niobium_titanium_rf_amplifier",
      "text": "$(item)RF Amplifiers$() are used to increase plasma energy with radio-frequency waves (like a microwave). In other words, they heat up the plasma. The leftovers do not reheat well."
    },
    {
